{title: For All the Saints}
{artist: William How & Ralph Vaughan Williams}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
For [G]all the saints who [C]from their [G]labors [D]rest,
who [G]thee by [C]faith be[G]fore the [D]world con[Em]fessed,
thy [C]name, O Jesus, [G]be for[D]ever [Em]blessed:
alle[G]luia! [D]Alle[G]luia!

Verse 2
Thou wast [C]their [D]Rock,
their Fortress [G]and their [Em]Might;
Thou, [C]Lord, their Captain in [G]the well [D]fought [Em]fight;
[G]Thou, in the darkness drear, [D]their one true Light.

Verse 3
For the Apostles' glorious [D]company,
Who bearing forth [Em]the
Cross o'er land [G]and [Em]sea,
[G]Shook all the mighty world, [D]we sing to Thee:

Verse 4
The [G]golden evening brightens [C]in [G]the [D]west;
Soon, soon to [Em]faithful
warriors comes [G]their [Em]rest;
[G]Sweet is the calm [D]of paradise the blessed.

Verse 5
But lo! [C]there [D]breaks
a yet [G]more glorious [Em]day;
The [C]saints triumphant rise [G]in [D]bright [Em]array;
[G]The King of glory [D]passes on His way.
